# Telemetry. GuiProvider mounts it for you — there is no telemetry code in this
# app — but the door needs to know WHICH ORG a beacon belongs to, and that is
# the one value a build has to supply.
#
# PUBLISHABLE_KEY is the name the fleet already carries: KMS holds it at
# `deploy/PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, and every surface passes that one value through
# under its bundler's public prefix. Vite's is VITE_.
#
# It is a PUBLISHABLE key (`pk-…`): write-only, HMAC-verified to an org
# server-side, and safe to ship in a bundle — the same trust class as a Stripe
# publishable key. It is still a secret in the sense that it belongs in KMS and
# in CI, never in git.
#
# Leave it unset and the app runs fine; its beacons are simply unattributed and
# the door refuses them.
VITE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Optional. The product name is resolved from the runtime (a Tauri window
# reports as `desktop`), so set this only to override it.
# VITE_HANZO_PRODUCT=desktop

# Optional kill switch: 0 | false | off disables telemetry entirely.
# VITE_HANZO_TELEMETRY=
